%I A398926 #12 Sep 16 2026 00:26:16
%S A398926 1,1,1,4,185,169146,12009737846,1802445357594713999
%N A398926 Number of strict T1 closure systems on n labeled points with a fixed extreme point.
%C A398926 For a closure system on X, x is extreme if x is not in cl(X\{x}), and non-extreme if x is in cl(X\{x}).
%C A398926 The complementary case is when the fixed point is non-extreme; together the two cases partition A334255(n).
%H A398926 Dmitry I. Ignatov, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.12256">On the Cryptomorphism between Davis' Subset Lattices, Atomic Lattices, and Closure Systems under T1 Separation Axiom</a>, arXiv:2209.12256 [cs.DM], 2022.
%H A398926 Sonja Mapes, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1009.1430">Finite atomic lattices and resolutions of monomial ideals</a>, arXiv:1009.1430 [math.AC], 2010; J. Algebra 379 (2013), 259-276.
%F A398926 a(n) = Sum_{T in T_1(n-1)} g(T), where T_1(m) is the set of strict T1 closure systems on m labeled points and g(T) is the number of strict closure subsystems contained in T.
%F A398926 a(n) = A334255(n) - A398927(n).
%e A398926 Taking 3 as the fixed point, the a(3)=4 closure systems are {{1,2,3},{1,2},{1},{2},{3},{}}, {{1,2,3},{1,2},{1,3},{1},{2},{3},{}}, {{1,2,3},{1,2},{2,3},{1},{2},{3},{}}, {{1,2,3},{1,2},{1,3},{2,3},{1},{2},{3},{}}.
%Y A398926 Cf. A334255 (strict T1 closure systems on n labeled points), A398927 (strict T1 closure systems on n labeled points with a fixed non-extreme point).
%K A398926 nonn,more,new
%O A398926 0,4
%A A398926 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 11 2026
